.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd September 29, 2026
.Dt GETSOCKOPT 2
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm getsockopt ,
.Nm setsockopt
.Nd get and set options on sockets
.Sh LIBRARY
.Lb libc
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/socket.h
.Ft int
.Fo getsockopt
.Fa "int s"
.Fa "int level"
.Fa "int optname"
.Fa "void *restrict optval"
.Fa "socklen_t *restrict optlen"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo setsockopt
.Fa "int s"
.Fa "int level"
.Fa "int optname"
.Fa "const void *optval"
.Fa "socklen_t optlen"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These calls read and set the option
.Fa optname
at protocol level
.Fa level
on the socket
.Fa s .
The level is
.Dv SOL_SOCKET
for options of the socket itself, a protocol number such as
.Dv IPPROTO_TCP
for a protocol's options, or
.Dv SOL_LOCAL
for local sockets' options.
.Pp
.Fn setsockopt
sets the option from the
.Fa optlen
bytes at
.Fa optval .
.Fn getsockopt
stores the option's value at
.Fa optval ,
at most
.Fa *optlen
bytes of it, and sets
.Fa *optlen
to the number of bytes stored.
.Pp
Most options are an
.Vt int ,
zero for off and anything else for on.
.Ss Socket level
The options of level
.Dv SOL_SOCKET
are:
.Bl -tag -width SO_ACCEPTCONN
.It Dv SO_ACCEPTCONN
Whether the socket is listening.
Read only.
.It Dv SO_BROADCAST
Permission to send broadcast datagrams.
Recorded and reported, not yet acted on.
.It Dv SO_DOMAIN
The socket's domain, as given to
.Xr socket 2 .
Read only.
.It Dv SO_ERROR
The socket's pending error, or 0, which reading clears.
A non-blocking
.Xr connect 2
reports its result here.
Read only.
.It Dv SO_KEEPALIVE
Keep connections alive with periodic probes.
Recorded and reported, not yet acted on.
.It Dv SO_LINGER
A
.Vt struct linger
.Pq Va l_onoff , l_linger .
Recorded and reported, not yet acted on.
.It Dv SO_NOSIGPIPE
Do not raise
.Dv SIGPIPE
when a send or
.Xr write 2
on the socket fails with
.Er EPIPE .
.Fx Ns 's
option, with its value, 0x0800.
.It Dv SO_PASSCRED
Receive the sender's credentials with every message
.Pq local sockets ; see Xr unix 4 .
.It Dv SO_PEERCRED
The connected peer's credentials, a
.Vt struct ucred
.Pq local sockets ; see Xr unix 4 .
Read only.
.It Dv SO_PROTOCOL
The socket's protocol, as given to
.Xr socket 2 .
Read only.
.It Dv SO_RCVBUF
The size of the receive buffer: 64 KiB by default; values set are kept
between 512 bytes and 1 MiB.
Acted on by local sockets; recorded and reported by Internet sockets.
.It Dv SO_RCVLOWAT
The least data a receive waits for; at least 1.
Recorded and reported, not yet acted on.
.It Dv SO_RCVTIMEO
A
.Vt struct timeval :
how long a blocking receive or
.Xr accept 2
waits before failing with
.Er EAGAIN ;
zero, the default, waits indefinitely.
.It Dv SO_REUSEADDR
Allow reuse of local addresses.
Recorded and reported, not yet acted on.
.It Dv SO_SNDBUF
The size of the send buffer, as
.Dv SO_RCVBUF .
A local datagram larger than it fails with
.Er EMSGSIZE .
.It Dv SO_SNDTIMEO
As
.Dv SO_RCVTIMEO ,
for sends.
.It Dv SO_TYPE
The socket's type.
Read only.
.El
.Ss Internet levels
Internet sockets accept these options, which are recorded and reported
back but do not yet change the packets sent:
.Dv IP_TOS ,
.Dv IP_TTL ,
.Dv IP_MULTICAST_IF ,
.Dv IP_MULTICAST_TTL
and
.Dv IP_MULTICAST_LOOP
at level
.Dv IPPROTO_IP ,
and, on TCP sockets,
.Dv TCP_NODELAY
at level
.Dv IPPROTO_TCP ,
which reads as on until set, since every segment is sent at once.
.Ss Local level
.Dv LOCAL_PEERCRED ,
.Dv LOCAL_CREDS
and
.Dv LOCAL_CREDS_PERSISTENT
at level
.Dv SOL_LOCAL
are described in
.Xr unix 4 .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Rv -std
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er EBADF
.Fa s
is not an open descriptor.
.It Bq Er EINVAL
.Fa optlen
is
.Dv NULL
.Pq Fn getsockopt ,
the value is too short for the option, a time-out is negative or has
microseconds out of range, a local-socket option was used on a socket of
another family, both
.Dv LOCAL_CREDS
and
.Dv LOCAL_CREDS_PERSISTENT
would be set, or
.Dv LOCAL_PEERCRED
was set.
.It Bq Er ENOPROTOOPT
The option is unknown at that level, or read only and being set.
.It Bq Er ENOTCONN
.Dv SO_PEERCRED
or
.Dv LOCAL_PEERCRED
was read on a socket that was never connected.
.It Bq Er ENOTSOCK
.Fa s
is not a socket.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr socket 2 ,
.Xr unix 4
.Sh STANDARDS
These calls conform to
.St -p1003.1-2008 .
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn getsockopt
and
.Fn setsockopt
system calls first appeared in
.Bx 4.2 .
In OxideBSD they are system calls 579 and 580, each taking its level,
name, value and length in one structure, as the native system-call
interface passes at most four arguments; the former three-argument
.Fn setsockopt ,
144, is retired and fails with
.Er ENOSYS .
